   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Inferring from clues",
     "texto": [
      "**-(으)ㄴ 모양이다** also presents an inference: 바쁘다 → **바쁜 모양이에요**, 가다 → **간 모양이에요** (it seems (he/she) went), 오다 → **온 모양이에요** (it seems (he/she) came). With a verb in the present, use **-는 모양이다**: 가다 → **가는 모양이에요**.",
      "요즘 회사에 일이 많은 **모양이에요** = it seems there is a lot of work at the company lately."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Nuance and register",
     "texto": [
      "**-나 봐요** and **-(으)ㄴ/는 모양이에요** overlap as expressions of inference. **-나 봐요** is very common in conversation; **모양이다** can sound more descriptive or typical of written texts, but it is not simply a formal and objective version in every context."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
